## Spatial, temporal, textural, transition, pressure/release, and recurrence maps

- **Spatial:** mandarin is the near-field pressure cap; ginger traverses front-to-center; violet cloth forms the middle shell; tonka is an interior chamber; cedar/vetiver is the back wall; floral air is the negative space.
- **Temporal:** 0–5 min juicy peel/ginger; 5–30 min green pith and violet cloth; 30–120 min hay aperture; 2–6 h yielding tonka/sandal; 6–24 h dry cedar-root recurrence. All are modeled intentions, **NOT TESTED**.
- **Nineteen conserved textures:** polished; waxed; wet-cut; juicy; crisp; fatty; fibrous; tailored-cloth; leafy; metallic; bitter; humid; mineral; pencil-dry; rooty; hayed; creamy-yielding; textile; slow.
- **Pressure/release:** red mandarin presses outward; green pith and violet cloth restrain it; floral air releases the middle; coumarinic warmth presses inward; sandal yields; dry woods release as an echo.
- **Ten transition/recurrence links:** (1) peel→ginger, (2) ginger→green pith, (3) pith→violet cloth, (4) violet→floral air, (5) air→hay aperture, (6) hay→tonka chamber, (7) tonka→sandal yield, (8) sandal→cedar wall, (9) cedar→vetiver echo, (10) peel dryness→patchouli/benzoate recurrence.

