## Missing-chemical impact gate

|Ideal-only / held state|Impact if absent from current|Current decision|
|---|---|---|
|Polysantol|Ideal slow sandal curvature is unavailable|Omit; Sandalore/Ebanol are the bounded current yielding faces, not chemical equivalence|
|Violet Leaf Absolute 10%|Natural green shadow loses nuance because local physics is incomplete|Omit; Parmavert/Leafovert own the executable green seam|
|Ginger CO2, Hedione HC, Haitian vetiver|Ideal oily rhizome, high-cis lift, and clean root highlight are not required for the primary axis|Omit without claiming equivalence|
|Opoponax/Myrrh 50% basis-HOLD states|Could darken the chamber but exact active arithmetic is unsupported|Omit from executable and all ppm/OAV math|
|Piconia, Methyl Laitone, resin/aldehyde traces|Optional polish may deepen the ideal|Omit until isolated value is demonstrated|
|Romandolide / Ethylene Brassylate|Could add continuity but would change the zero-musk hypothesis|Omit from primary; future diagnostic only|

**Gate result:** executable structure remains interpretable without these rows. No missing chemical forces target-identity collapse. This is a design judgment, **NOT TESTED**.

## Future mixing order

If and only if later authorized: (1) Sandalore/Ebanol, cedar, vetiver, and patchouli chamber; (2) Tonka Bean Absolute 10% DPG; (3) violet/green cloth; (4) bounded floral air; (5) ginger; (6) red mandarin last; (7) alcohol phase. Record masses, temperatures, stock labels, order, clarity, and losses. Tonkarome and Coumarin are absent from this executable order. This is **no compounding authorization** and makes no stability claim.

## Controlled blinded test plan

Primary screen: independently prepare current stock-corrected L'Homme V6 control and LH-03 at constant 6,000 uL concentrate total, equal final concentration, and carrier-matched alcohol/DEP/DPG/TEC composition. Use two independently prepared complete sets, anonymous codes, counterbalanced AB/BA order, equal substrate, and free description before scoring. Evaluate at 0, 5, 30, 120 minutes, 6 hours, and 24 hours.

Separate criteria: opening pleasure; juicy peel clarity; ginger warmth; violet tailoring; hayed transition; chamber depth; sandal/cedar echo; transition pleasure; drydown pleasure; overall liking; re-smell desire; muddiness; dessert, pastry, syrup, powder, or LNDL-spice defects. A computational score or one assessor cannot establish success.

**Future chamber-film diagnostic only:** if natural-tonka continuity remains a specifically observed deficit, compare LH-03 with a constant-total arm replacing 200 uL of Tonka Bean Absolute 10% DPG with 200 uL Ethylene Brassylate plus an exact 180 uL DPG compensation in every arm. This tests film versus natural chamber only; it is not a recommendation, equivalence claim, or primary-formula revision.

